Title: Test Script

INT. KITCHEN - NIGHT #1#

Yasmin stirs a pot. The radio crackles with news from Jenin.

NIDAL (V.O.)
Is the bread ready? We leave for Nablus before the checkpoint closes.

YASMIN
(not looking up)
Not yet. Your mother wanted the olives packed first, and the jars are still wet.

NIDAL
Then we take the jars wet. The soldiers will not wait for olives.

CUT TO:

EXT. CHECKPOINT - DAY #2#

A long queue of cars in the heat. A SOLDIER walks the line.

SOLDIER
Papers. Everyone out of the car.

NIDAL
We are going to my uncle's wedding in Nablus. My cousin Karim is getting married.

SOLDIER
Open the trunk.

YASMIN
They are only olives, and a cake for the bride. Please be careful with the cake.

INT. UNCLE'S HOUSE - NIGHT #3#

Music. Dancing. KARIM, 30s, hugs Nidal.

KARIM
You made it! I told everyone the checkpoint would stop you.

NIDAL
The soldier wanted to eat the cake.
